WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.112
Step 6 routes the same collection
again, on a copy of the state.

2
00:00:04.112 --> 00:00:07.793
All twenty-two are unchanged,
so nothing is written:

3
00:00:07.793 --> 00:00:11.825
no payloads, because nothing
new or changed needs a task.

4
00:00:11.825 --> 00:00:13.688
That's what keeps the queue readable.

5
00:00:13.688 --> 00:00:16.626
Step 7 collects and
routes the second week.

6
00:00:16.626 --> 00:00:22.588
Two notices are new, six changed, fifteen
unchanged, and one is no longer listed.

7
00:00:22.588 --> 00:00:28.412
The router writes just six payloads:
one create, four updates and one close.

8
00:00:28.412 --> 00:00:32.531
The routing hasn't changed, so the
same twelve notices route to tasks,

9
00:00:32.531 --> 00:00:35.980
but only the six with something
new to say make a payload.
